          "explanation": "The historical facts (party membership, Rectoral Address, Black Notebooks content) are well-documented and not seriously disputed among historians. What remains genuinely contested among philosophers is the interpretive question of how much weight those facts should carry in evaluating his philosophical work — a live debate, not a settled one, and Heidegger never issued an unambiguous apology.",
